*  gim_cassign_array_elt_loud - the LOUD SIBLING, one character apart from
*  gim_defer_cassign_array_elt: the same array-element capture target WITHOUT
*  the '*'.  SCRIP refuses it honestly --
*    FATAL lower_snobol4 (GZ#5 subset): capture target in a runtime-built
*    pattern is not a simple variable.
*  So the defect is not "unlanded": it is that the DEFER SPELLING BYPASSES THE
*  REFUSAL.  A feature declared unlanded must fail on EVERY path that reaches
*  it (gimpel batch A, EVAL/CONVERT class).  No .ref: SCRIP is expected to
*  refuse, the oracle prints [x].
        A  =  ARRAY(1)
        I  =  1
        S  =  'xyz'
        S  LEN(1) . A<I>  =
        OUTPUT  =  '[' A<1> ']'
END
